{"s":[[null,1,[["p",["There are two distinct Speed statistics:"]],["l",0,[[1,[["f","Speed_w.png",24]," Weapon Speed refers to how long it takes to hit an enemy with a weapon."]],[1,[["f","Speed.png",24]," Player Speed refers to how fast the player moves."]]]],["p",["Each can be affected in a variety of ways."]]]],["Weapon Speed",2,[["p",["Weapon Speed refers to how long it takes to hit an enemy with a weapon, and how long it takes to recover before hitting again."]],["p",["By default with +0 Weapon Speed, ",["l","武器#Sword","swords"]," take 400 milliseconds per action and ",["l","武器#Club","clubs"]," take 720 milliseconds per action (equivalent to -8 buff). ",["l","武器#Dagger","Daggers"]," are much faster than swords. ",["l","武器#Slingshot","Slingshots"]," take 300 milliseconds per action and cannot be modified."]],["p",["Each point of Weapon Speed reduces the time taken by 40 milliseconds, meaning the maximum effective buff is +10 for swords, though the practical performance limit may be lower (maximum effective buff of around +4 for swords or +12 for clubs)."]],["p",["This also means that at first, Weapon Speed has a significantly smaller effect on clubs because the total increase in damage per second (when striking continuously) is smaller as a percentage: a sword with +1 Weapon Speed is capable of 11% more damage per second, whereas a club with +1 Weapon Speed is only capable of 6% more damage per second. As buff increases, swords hit the practical performance limit faster, and clubs continue improving with higher buff."]],["p",["The player's movement speed buff (described below) is also applied to weapons, and effectively stacks with the Weapon Speed buff. For example, a weapon with speed +2 would be just as fast as a weapon with speed +1 while under the effects of ",["l","咖啡","Coffee"]," for an additional +1."]]]],["Weapons",3,[["p",["The following ",["l","武器","Weapons"]," swipe faster or slower than normal."]],["t",[[{"h":1,"v":["Image"]},{"h":1,"v":["Name"]},{"h